and for the first time we're hearing  from the family of a man who was shot  and killed by police this all happened a  month ago right near nellis in vegas  valley police were there serving a  search warrant and once inside they were  met by gunfire but the family tells 8  news now is victoria saha it was all  self-defense and she joins us from the  newsroom with this exclusive interview  isaiah williams was 19 when he was  killed last month in a shootout with  metro police his mom is still heavily  grieving but wants answers from metro  because she says her son did not deserve  to die  this body cam footage released by police  shows the moments before officers kicked  down the door to serve their search  warrant and met by gunfire from isaiah  williams  his mom latia alexander is still trying  to comprehend the situation for the  moment of me watching the video  i just  froze up i was shaking so bad police  were issuing a search warrant for a  suspect connected to a murder that  happened back in november police say  williams fired 18 times at officers and  between five of them 23 rounds were  fired back at williams body cam footage  shows williams was laying on the couch  with a gun right by the door do you  believe that he didn't hear police the  police saying their presence i honestly  believe that he did not hear it his mom  says williams was a heavy sleeper and  missed curfew that night and slept at  his friend's apartment uncomfortable in  a new environment he slept with a gun by  his side he was scared for sure she says  he was not connected to the suspect  police were looking for and the suspect  did not live there no we weren't in the  wrong address angered by the intensity  of the situation his family demanded  answers by protesting at a police forum  thursday evening they did not deserve to  die his mom wants everyone to know the  body cam footage does not define who her  son was for years old like the older the  elderly if he see him take the garbage  he'll go grab the garbage take the  garbage out  police did admit williams was not the  person they were looking for the right  suspect was arrested a few days after  that incident two officers were shot but  one officer still has a long road to  recovery as for williams's mom she's  still waiting for police documents and  the coroner's report so she can pay to  lay her son to rest brian
 

